  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nTuesday an upper trough along the west coast will begin to move\ninland and turn the flow over TX to the southwest. At the same\ntime the low level flow will continue from the southeast and \nmoisture in the vertical will increase. We will see showers \ndevelop during the afternoon both Tuesday and Wednesday. Chances \nfor rain will spread from the Coastal Plains to the eastern Hill\nCountry. In addition to the rain chances, temperatures will \nincrease into the middle of the week. With the higher humidity \nheat indices will push back above 100 degrees for most of the CWA\nTuesday and Wednesday. There will probably be some places that\nreach Heat Advisory criteria, but these conditions will not be\nwidespread. Models continue to move the upper trough across the \ncentral Rockies and into the Plains bringing a cold front through\nSouth-Central Texas. They seem to be getting more consistent with\nthe rain chances later in the week with the possibility of locally\nheavy rain Thursday night/Friday. Behind the front temperatures\nwill be lower Friday through Sunday. Low temperatures next weekend\ncould be in the 50s and highs in the 70s for most of the area.",
